## Merge hygiene (optional - only if several sessions / PRs work this repo in parallel)
- Derived / generated files (<GENERATED_FILES>, e.g. lockfile, generated types, pin/snapshot files)
  are regenerated after merge, never hand-merged. If one conflicts, take the base side first,
  then regenerate (<REGEN_CMD>) and commit the result. Files where both sides add entries
  (e.g. type definitions) keep BOTH sides' additions; prove it with <TYPECHECK_CMD>.
- After merging the base branch, check that no two PRs redefined the same object (e.g. the
  same DB function replaced in two migrations) - if so, stop and reconcile.
- Sibling PRs cut from one base merge in their apply order, each stacked on the previous PR's
  resolved head (never re-resolve the same conflict twice).
- Merge the base branch into your branch before opening its PR; aim to merge within ~3 days of branching.
- No PR appends to a shared single-line registry (e.g. one long `"test"` script line) - derive it
  instead (a runner that discovers `*.test.*` files), so a PR only adds files.

